Description: error on a check rollup page that claims more rows without a cursor
Author: Azhou AI Hub
Forwarded: no

The rollup reader folded "hasNextPage is true but there is no endCursor" into
"there are no more checks", so the walk stopped at page one and every check past
the first hundred disappeared. A pull request with a failing check on page two
was read as clean and reported ready to merge. The parser now raises that page as
a query error instead of truncating, and it is a named parser so the boundary is
covered by a test the way the review thread and pull request parsers already are.

